 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 504777,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the LCM of 18, 24, and 40 using lists and prime factorization.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Using lists:</p>\n<p>List multiples of each number until you find a common number.</p>\n<p>18: 18, 36, 54, 72, 90, 108, 126, 144, 162, 180, 198, 216, 234, 252, 270, 288, 306, 324, 342, 360</p>\n<p>24: 24, 48, 72, 120, 144, 168, 192, 216, 240, 264, 288, 312, 336, 360</p>\n<p>40: 40, 80, 120, 160, 200, 240, 280, 320, 360</p>\n<p>The first common number is 360. The LCM is 360.</p>\n<p>Using prime factorization:</p>\n<p>Find the prime factorization of each number.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"18 = 2 \\times {3^2}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"24 = {2^3} \\times 3\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"40 = {2^3} \\times 5\"></span></p>\n<p>Make a table of each prime and the largest exponent for each prime.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Prime</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Exponent</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The LCM is the product of each prime raised to the powers identified in the table.</p>\n<p>The LCM is <span data-math=\"{2^3} \\times {3^2} \\times 5 = 360\"></span>.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "360"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
